  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome of each lottery and its probability, effectively comparing the product of the highest outcome and its probability. The individual considered the highest outcomes (2500 vs. 2400) and their probabilities (33% vs. 34%), and made a trade-off between the 100 Euro gain and 1% probability difference. While the individual did not explicitly compute expected values or state they focused only on the maximum outcome, their deliberation aligns with evaluating the weighted value of the best outcome: they weighed 100 Euros of extra gain against a 1% lower chance. This matches the core logic of the decision reason, which favors A due to the higher weighted value of its maximum outcome (825 > 816). Although the phrasing 'potential added value of 100€ over 1%' is somewhat ambiguous, it is consistent with the reasoning rule. There is no indication of considering other aspects (e.g., expected value of all outcomes, risk attitude, or certainty effects). The focus on the top outcome and its probability strongly suggests use of the specified reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

