  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome of each lottery weighted by its probability (i.e., 3000×0.25=750 vs. 4000×0.20=800), and would prefer Lottery B. However, the individual’s reasoning emphasizes the higher probability of winning in Lottery A and downplays the value of the higher outcome in B. The individual does not mention or compute the product of the maximum outcome and its probability, nor do they indicate that they evaluated the 'favorability' of the largest outcome based on this weighted value. Instead, they treat probability and outcome as separate factors in a trade-off, giving more weight to probability. There is no indication that the maximum magnitude outcome was evaluated in the manner specified by the reason (i.e., as a weighted value). Therefore, the individual’s information use and decision rule differ from those of the stated reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
