  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome (in absolute value) and favors the lottery where the most extreme outcome (in magnitude) is more favorable (i.e., positive) and weighted by its probability. In this case, it would attend to the 3000 Euro outcome in Lottery B (larger magnitude than 1500) and consider its 50% chance. However, the individual does not reference large outcomes, extremes, or magnitudes. Instead, the justification is based on preferring certainty and avoiding potential losses—indicative of risk aversion or a certainty effect, not a focus on extreme gains. The individual avoids Lottery B because of the potential loss, not because of any evaluation of the large possible gain. There is no evidence that the maximum magnitude outcome or its probabilistic weight was considered. Therefore, the information and rule underlying the decision reason are not reflected in the verbal report.",
